            <div xml:id="d685">

                <pb facs="0739" n="727" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg727"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.852/54: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-04-05T14:00:00-03:00">April 5, 1943—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 5:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1648. Department’s 1220, April 3, 7 p.m.<anchor n="47" xml:id="d685-f1"/> Aranha
                    told me this morning that notwithstanding the determined opposition of various
                    of his colleagues who say that Brazil needs the ITA ships more than we do, he
                    will go ahead with at least a part of the deal on Wednesday next.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
